---
layout: layouts/feature.njk
centered: true
wide: true
playgroundCta: true
hideBreadcrumbs: true
title: Features | Shellui
description: "The Shellui host: a microfrontend shell, authentication, an embedded admin, private company file storage, and optional Tauri desktop bundles."
heading: What the shell ships
lede: Four host surfaces wrap your application. You bring the iframe app. The same project can also ship as a native desktop app.
---

<div class="grid gap-6 lg:gap-8">
  <a
    href="/features/microfrontend/"
    class="group grid overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-gray-200 bg-white focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-primary dark:border-gray-800 dark:bg-gray-900 lg:grid-cols-2"
  >
    <div class="flex flex-col justify-center p-8 sm:p-10 lg:p-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-gray-900 sm:text-3xl dark:text-white">Microfrontend</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-base/7 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">Host your app in an iframe. Load the SDK, call init, and talk to the shell over postMessage. Chrome stays in the host: layouts, toasts, dialogs, theme, and language.</p>
      <ul class="mt-6 space-y-2 text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">
        <li>Sidebar, top bar, or window layout</li>
        <li>Toast, dialog, modal, and drawer from the SDK</li>
        <li>One <code class="rounded bg-gray-100 px-1 py-0.5 text-[0.8rem] dark:bg-gray-800">shellui.config.json</code></li>
      </ul>
      <span class="mt-8 inline-flex items-center text-sm font-medium text-primary-ink group-hover:underline dark:text-primary">Explore microfrontend</span>
    </div>
    <div class="flex items-center bg-gray-50 p-8 dark:bg-gray-950/60 sm:p-10">
      <div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-md">
        {% include "shell-layout-anim.njk" %}
      </div>
    </div>
  </a>

  <a
    href="/features/authentication/"
    class="group grid overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-gray-200 bg-white focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-primary dark:border-gray-800 dark:bg-gray-900 lg:grid-cols-2"
  >
    <div class="order-2 flex items-center bg-gray-50 p-8 dark:bg-gray-950/60 sm:p-10 lg:order-1">
      <div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-xs">
        {% include "feature-visual-auth.njk" %}
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="order-1 flex flex-col justify-center p-8 sm:p-10 lg:order-2 lg:p-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-gray-900 sm:text-3xl dark:text-white">Authentication</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-base/7 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">Sign-in lives in the shell. Connect identity-service or Supabase, protect routes, and decide who can join: public, a domain allow list, or invitation only.</p>
      <ul class="mt-6 space-y-2 text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">
        <li>OAuth, JWT sessions, and JSON Web Key Set (JWKS)</li>
        <li>Groups and login logs</li>
        <li>Access tokens for users and services</li>
      </ul>
      <span class="mt-8 inline-flex items-center text-sm font-medium text-primary-ink group-hover:underline dark:text-primary">Explore authentication</span>
    </div>
  </a>

  <a
    href="/features/administration/"
    class="group grid overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-gray-200 bg-white focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-primary dark:border-gray-800 dark:bg-gray-900 lg:grid-cols-2"
  >
    <div class="flex flex-col justify-center p-8 sm:p-10 lg:p-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-gray-900 sm:text-3xl dark:text-white">Administration</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-base/7 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">Staff and company owners open an embedded admin from the account menu. Manage the directory there, then inject your own apps into the sidebar from config.</p>
      <ul class="mt-6 space-y-2 text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">
        <li>Users, organization, and join modes</li>
        <li>Groups, logs, tokens, and OAuth clients</li>
        <li>Custom admin navigation</li>
      </ul>
      <span class="mt-8 inline-flex items-center text-sm font-medium text-primary-ink group-hover:underline dark:text-primary">Explore administration</span>
    </div>
    <div class="flex items-center bg-gray-50 p-8 dark:bg-gray-950/60 sm:p-10">
      <div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-sm">
        {% include "feature-visual-admin.njk" %}
      </div>
    </div>
  </a>

  <a
    href="/features/storage/"
    class="group grid overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-gray-200 bg-white focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-primary dark:border-gray-800 dark:bg-gray-900 lg:grid-cols-2"
  >
    <div class="order-2 flex items-center bg-gray-50 p-8 dark:bg-gray-950/60 sm:p-10 lg:order-1">
      <div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-xs">
        {% include "feature-visual-storage.njk" %}
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="order-1 flex flex-col justify-center p-8 sm:p-10 lg:order-2 lg:p-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-gray-900 sm:text-3xl dark:text-white">Storage</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-base/7 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">A company bucket behind the shell. New files stay private until you share them. Iframe apps upload, list, and pick files through <code class="rounded bg-gray-100 px-1 py-0.5 text-[0.8rem] dark:bg-gray-800">shellui.storage</code>.</p>
      <ul class="mt-6 space-y-2 text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">
        <li>Access grants for users, groups, or the company</li>
        <li>Share links with expiry and download caps</li>
        <li>Company and per-user quotas</li>
      </ul>
      <span class="mt-8 inline-flex items-center text-sm font-medium text-primary-ink group-hover:underline dark:text-primary">Explore storage</span>
    </div>
  </a>
</div>

<section id="desktop" class="mt-16 border-t border-gray-200 pt-16 dark:border-gray-800 sm:mt-20 sm:pt-20">
  <div class="max-w-2xl">
    <h2 class="flex items-center gap-3 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-gray-900 sm:text-3xl dark:text-white">
      {% set tauriIconClass = "size-7 sm:size-8" %}
      {% include "tauri-icon.njk" %}
      Desktop app with Tauri
    </h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base/7 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">
      Ship the same shell as a native desktop app. The CLI uses Tauri 2, writes the wrapper into <code class="rounded bg-gray-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm dark:bg-gray-800">dist/app/</code>, and keeps native project files out of your repo. Static web and desktop share one config and one iframe app.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="mt-10 grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:gap-16">
    <div>
      <h3 class="flex items-center gap-2 text-base font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">
        {% set tauriIconClass = "size-4" %}
        {% include "tauri-icon.njk" %}
        Commands
      </h3>
      <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2 text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">
        <li><code class="rounded bg-gray-100 px-1 py-0.5 text-[0.8rem] dark:bg-gray-800">shellui dev --app</code> opens a native window in development</li>
        <li><code class="rounded bg-gray-100 px-1 py-0.5 text-[0.8rem] dark:bg-gray-800">shellui build --app</code> emits <code class="rounded bg-gray-100 px-1 py-0.5 text-[0.8rem] dark:bg-gray-800">dist/web/</code> plus a platform bundle under <code class="rounded bg-gray-100 px-1 py-0.5 text-[0.8rem] dark:bg-gray-800">dist/app/</code></li>
        <li>Pass <code class="rounded bg-gray-100 px-1 py-0.5 text-[0.8rem] dark:bg-gray-800">--bundles</code> for formats such as <code class="rounded bg-gray-100 px-1 py-0.5 text-[0.8rem] dark:bg-gray-800">app,dmg</code> on macOS</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="mt-6 max-w-xl">
        {% highlight "bash", "terminal" %}
shellui build --app
        {% endhighlight %}
      </div>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">What you bring</h3>
      <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2 text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">
        <li>Rust via rustup, plus the usual Tauri platform prerequisites</li>
        <li>Optional root <code class="rounded bg-gray-100 px-1 py-0.5 text-[0.8rem] dark:bg-gray-800">tauri.conf.json</code> for product name, identifier, and icons</li>
        <li><code class="rounded bg-gray-100 px-1 py-0.5 text-[0.8rem] dark:bg-gray-800">port</code> and <code class="rounded bg-gray-100 px-1 py-0.5 text-[0.8rem] dark:bg-gray-800">title</code> from <code class="rounded bg-gray-100 px-1 py-0.5 text-[0.8rem] dark:bg-gray-800">shellui.config.json</code> sync into the wrapper</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-6 text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400">
        <a href="{{ site.docs }}/tauri/" class="font-medium text-primary-ink hover:underline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-primary dark:text-primary">Ship a desktop app</a>
        ·
        <a href="/#config" class="font-medium text-primary-ink hover:underline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-primary dark:text-primary">One config file</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
